  "notes": "{傷|きず} refers to wounds, scratches, or flaws - physical damage or imperfections.\n\nMEANINGS:\n1. Physical injury: {傷|きず}を{負|お}う (to get injured)\n2. Surface damage: {車|くるま}に{傷|きず}がつく (car gets scratched)\n3. Abstract flaw: {評判|ひょうばん}に{傷|きず}がつく (reputation is damaged)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {傷|きず}がつく: to get scratched/damaged\n- {傷|きず}を{負|お}う: to sustain an injury\n- {傷|きず}が{治|なお}る: wound heals\n- {傷|きず}を{手当|てあ}てする: to treat a wound\n\nTYPES OF WOUNDS:\n- {切|き}り{傷|きず}: cut\n- {擦|す}り{傷|きず}: scrape, abrasion\n- {火傷|やけど}: burn\n- {打撲傷|だぼくしょう}: bruise\n\nCOMPOUNDS:\n- {傷跡|きずあと}: scar\n- {傷口|きずぐち}: wound opening\n- {無傷|むきず}: uninjured, unscathed\n- {古傷|ふるきず}: old wound\n\nIDIOM:\n{玉|たま}に{傷|きず}: a fly in the ointment (lit: a flaw in a jewel)",
